    "result_text": "All clean. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) across the app:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` string field for `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 4`, `readOnly`), which regenerates the `OwnerDto` accessor. This removes `membershipTier` from the response in favour of `membershipLevel`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced `getMembershipTier()` with a derived `getMembershipLevel()`: starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (leaving level 4 for tenure). MapStruct maps this onto the DTO automatically since the names match.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `applyHouseholdMembershipTier` `@AfterMapping` (and its `HouseholdMembershipTierEvaluator` dependency). That logic only existed to override the now-removed tier with `GOLD`; the new level is defined purely by the owner's own email/namesake fields, so household size no longer applies.\n- **`HouseholdMembershipTierEvaluator.java`** \u2014 deleted, since it was only used by the removed override (avoiding dead code).\n- **`OwnerAuditLogger.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel` instead of the tier.\n\nEach piece stayed in its existing home: the derivation rule on the entity, the response-only concerns in the mapper, the audit fact in the audit logger. `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, and the audit output confirms `membershipLevel=3` for an emailed, uniquely-named owner.\n\nA note on one judgment call: the existing create audit line did **not** actually record the old tier, so \"record the level instead\" had nothing to literally replace. Since the spec explicitly named the create audit line as the thing that should carry the level, I added `membershipLevel` to it. If you'd rather leave the audit line untouched, that's a one-line revert.",
